{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And its saying</b> further, <b>When a man is found lying</b> etc. — it may be explained according to the words of the Sages, whose memory is for blessing (Sanhedrin 59a), who said: a gentile who engages in Torah is liable to death, end quote. And this is the meaning of <b>When a man is found lying with a woman</b> who is betrothed to her husband — she being the Torah, the bride of Israel — <b>and both of them shall die</b>, meaning: the gentile who engages with it, and also that Torah — it shall have no ascent, rather its lamp shall be extinguished, and it has no vitality in the manner of the words of Torah, as it is written (Proverbs 4:22): ״כִּי חַיִּים הֵם״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:18:32.976033656Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}